---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Work"
  description="Verified Drimini work, with the decisions, constraints, and limitations left visible."
>
  <header class="page-intro shell">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Selected work</p>
      <h1>Work we can show honestly.</h1>
    </div>
    <p>
      Drimini is new. These are our own projects, not borrowed client stories. We
      publish them because the reasoning, implementation, and limits are inspectable.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="work-index shell" aria-labelledby="work-index-title">
    <h2 class="visually-hidden" id="work-index-title">Available projects</h2>
    <article class="work-card work-card--large">
      <div class="work-card__meta">
        <span>Self-initiated</span>
        <span>Live / 2026</span>
      </div>
      <div class="work-card__body">
        <div>
          <p class="work-card__kicker">Website + contact operations</p>
          <h3>Drimini website and contact system</h3>
        </div>
        <p>
          How we framed, built, hardened, and now operate Drimini's first public
          product without inventing scale, proof, or a bigger company behind it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul class="work-card__facts" aria-label="Project highlights">
        <li>Astro static site</li>
        <li>Cloudflare Pages + D1</li>
        <li>Human-owned enquiry operations</li>
        <li>Automated accessibility checks</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="work-card__link" href="/work/drimini-website">
        Read website case study <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </article>

    <article class="work-card work-card--large work-card--experiment">
      <div class="work-card__meta">
        <span>Experimental / Open source</span>
        <span>Preview / 2026</span>
      </div>
      <div class="work-card__body">
        <div>
          <p class="work-card__kicker">Release + handover tooling</p>
          <h3>Release Evidence</h3>
        </div>
        <p>
          A local-first workbench that scans repository evidence, keeps machine
          observations separate from human judgment, and leaves the release
          decision with its owner.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul class="work-card__facts" aria-label="Project highlights">
        <li>Go + local web interface</li>
        <li>Offline by default</li>
        <li>Apache-2.0 source</li>
        <li>Independent validation pending</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="work-card__link" href="/work/release-evidence">
        Explore Release Evidence <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="contact-callout" aria-labelledby="work-contact-title">
    <div class="shell contact-callout__inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Your difficult bit</p>
      <h2 id="work-contact-title">Need this level of ownership?</h2>
      <p>Tell us what needs to work, what is getting in the way, and why it matters.</p>
      <a class="button button--dark" href="/contact">Contact us <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
